VeridianOS: FindKSystemStats names its results after the package, and
looks in the target system

cmake/FindKSystemStats.cmake passed "ksystemstats" to
find_package_handle_standard_args() for find_package(KSystemStats), which
CMake reports ("The package name passed to
find_package_handle_standard_args() (ksystemstats) does not match the name
of the calling package (KSystemStats)"), and which set ksystemstats_FOUND
rather than the KSystemStats_FOUND the feature summary reads. The results
are now named after the package.

ksystemstats is a run-time dependency (the system monitor talks to it); a
cross build found the build host's /usr/bin/ksystemstats, as programs are
looked up on the host. When cross compiling it is now looked up in the
target's root (CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH), where it is installed.

--- a/cmake/FindKSystemStats.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindKSystemStats.cmake
@@ -1,10 +1,15 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2021 David Redondo <kde@david-redondo.de>
 
-find_program(ksystemstats_EXE ksystemstats)
+# A run-time dependency: when cross compiling, the target's program.
+if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
+    find_program(KSystemStats_EXE ksystemstats ONLY_CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH)
+else()
+    find_program(KSystemStats_EXE ksystemstats)
+endif()
 
 include(FindPackageHandleStandardArgs)
-find_package_handle_standard_args(ksystemstats
-    FOUND_VAR ksystemstats_FOUND
-    REQUIRED_VARS ksystemstats_EXE
+find_package_handle_standard_args(KSystemStats
+    FOUND_VAR KSystemStats_FOUND
+    REQUIRED_VARS KSystemStats_EXE
 )
